        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Br\" means the element \"bromine\" and \"82mBr\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"bromine-82\" with a half-life of 4.24e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::1IXM3VKH";
