        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Th\" means the element \"thorium\" and \"231Th\" is the isotope \"thorium-231\" with a half-life of 1.06e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::Z6XWS17E";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_231Th_in_air"@en;
