<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N62/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N62";
        dc:date                "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N62";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-12-17 17:17:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N62/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N62/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_hydroperoxyl_radical/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_hydroperoxyl_radical>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G153/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used. The chemical formula for the hydroperoxyl radical is HO2. In chemistry, a 'radical' is a highly reactive, and therefore short lived, species."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N62";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_hydroperoxyl_radical"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/36UW7DBQ/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::36UW7DBQ";
        dc:date                "2026-09-15 05:36:53.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::36UW7DBQ";
        pav:authoredOn         "2026-09-15 05:36:53.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/36UW7DBQ/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/36UW7DBQ/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ocean_mass_content_of_demersal_fish_expressed_as_wet_weight/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. Demersal fish spend a fraction of their lives in close association with the seabed, feeding primarily on bottom organisms, they can carry out diel vertical migrations (e.g. cod). The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction \"A_expressed_as_B\", where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. Wet weight is the weight of a material, organism, or sample including its water (moisture) content, measured before drying."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::36UW7DBQ";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ocean_mass_content_of_demersal_fish_expressed_as_wet_weight"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UGMS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/91ED54E3/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::91ED54E3";
        dc:date                "2024-09-04 12:51:24.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::91ED54E3";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-09-04 12:51:24.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/91ED54E3/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/91ED54E3/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/91ED54E3/2/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/liquid_water_cloud_area_fraction/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/liquid_water_cloud_area_fraction>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Area fraction\" is the fraction of a grid cell's horizontal area that has some characteristic of interest. It is evaluated as the area of interest divided by the grid cell area, or if the cell_methods restricts the evaluation to some portion of that grid cell (e.g. \"where sea_ice\"), then it is the area of interest divided by the area of the identified portion. It may be expressed as a fraction, a percentage, or any other dimensionless representation of a fraction. The cloud area fraction is for the whole atmosphere column, as seen from the surface or the top of the atmosphere. For the cloud area fraction between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"cloud_area_fraction_in_atmosphere_layer\" are used. Standard names also exist for high, medium and low cloud types. \"Cloud area fraction is also called \"cloud amount\" and \"cloud cover\"."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::91ED54E3";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "liquid_water_cloud_area_fraction"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N429/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N429";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N429";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N429/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_beta_pinene_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_beta_pinene_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/OHAT/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G140/>;
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as 'nitrogen' or a phrase such as 'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen'. The chemical formula for beta_pinene is C10H16.  The IUPAC name for beta-pinene is (1S,5S)-6,6-dimethyl-2-methylenebicyclo[3.1.1]heptane."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N429";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_beta_pinene_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TJZAJESS/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::TJZAJESS";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::TJZAJESS";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:48.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TJZAJESS/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/volume_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm1_dry_aerosol_particles/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/volume_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm1_dry_aerosol_particles>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The volume scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is the fractional change of radiative flux per unit path length due to the stated process. Coefficients with canonical units of m2 s-1 i.e. multiplied by density have standard names with specific_ instead of volume_. A scattering_angle should not be specified with this quantity. The scattering/absorption/attenuation coefficient is assumed to be an integral over all wavelengths, unless a coordinate of radiation_wavelength is included to specify the wavelength. Radiative flux is the sum of shortwave and longwave radiative fluxes. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Pm1 aerosol particles\" means atmospheric particulate compounds with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 1 micrometers."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::TJZAJESS";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "volume_scattering_coefficient_of_radiative_flux_in_air_due_to_pm1_dry_aerosol_particles"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UPRM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N26/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV10N26";
        dc:date                "2008-10-21 10:00:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV10N26";
        pav:authoredOn         "2008-10-21 10:00:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N26/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/ocean_vertical_heat_diffusivity/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/ocean_vertical_heat_diffusivity>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G915/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G915/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Vertical heat diffusivity\" means the vertical component of the diffusivity of heat due to motion which is not resolved on the grid scale of the model."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV10N26";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "ocean_vertical_heat_diffusivity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/SQMS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KR1V8PXD/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::KR1V8PXD";
        dc:date                "2013-11-08 14:08:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::KR1V8PXD";
        pav:authoredOn         "2013-11-08 14:08:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/KR1V8PXD/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_volcanic_ash/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_volcanic_ash>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used. \"Volcanic_ash\" means the fine-grained products of explosive volcanic eruptions, such as minerals or crystals, older fragmented rock (e.g. andesite), and glass. Particles within a volcanic ash cloud have diameters less than 2 mm. \"Volcanic_ash\" does not include non-volcanic dust."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::KR1V8PXD";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_volcanic_ash"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/WKTGC2TB/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
