        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Ce\" means the element \"cerium\" and \"142Ce\" is the isotope \"cerium-142\" with a half-life of 1.82e+19 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::4AHLSQSM";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_142Ce_in_air"@en;
