<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2BJAV4MA/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::2BJAV4MA";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::2BJAV4MA";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/2BJAV4MA/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_85mKr_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_85mKr_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Kr\" means the element \"krypton\" and \"85mKr\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"krypton-85\" with a half-life of 1.83e-01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::2BJAV4MA";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_85mKr_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QJR38PP6/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::QJR38PP6";
        dc:date                "2020-09-14 20:42:12.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::QJR38PP6";
        pav:authoredOn         "2020-09-14 20:42:12.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/QJR38PP6/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_layer_thickness_expressed_as_geopotential_height_difference/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_layer_thickness_expressed_as_geopotential_height_difference>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The quantity with standard name atmosphere_layer_thickness_expressed_as_geopotential_height_difference is the difference of geopotential height between two atmospheric levels. \"Layer\" means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be \"model_level_number\", but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. \"Thickness\" means the vertical extent of a layer. Geopotential is the sum of the specific gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the specific centripetal potential energy. Geopotential height is the geopotential divided by the standard acceleration due to gravity. It is numerically similar to the altitude (or geometric height) and not to the quantity with standard name \"height\", which is relative to the surface."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::QJR38PP6";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_layer_thickness_expressed_as_geopotential_height_difference"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N486/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N486";
        dc:date                "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N486";
        pav:authoredOn         "2009-07-06 15:41:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N486/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_methyl_hydroperoxide_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_methyl_hydroperoxide_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Mole concentration means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.  A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as 'nitrogen' or a phrase such as 'nox_expressed_as_nitrogen'. The chemical formula for methyl hydroperoxide is CH3OOH."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N486";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_methyl_hydroperoxide_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/4ED55N1Q/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::4ED55N1Q";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::4ED55N1Q";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/4ED55N1Q/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pm2p5_sea_salt_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_wet_deposition/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A7LKPMP3/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pm2p5_sea_salt_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_wet_deposition>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the particles. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. \"Pm2p5 aerosol\" means atmospheric particulate compounds with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 2.5 micrometers. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Wet deposition\" means deposition by precipitation. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::4ED55N1Q";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pm2p5_sea_salt_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_wet_deposition"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A7LKPMP3/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::A7LKPMP3";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:30.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::A7LKPMP3";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:30.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A7LKPMP3/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A7LKPMP3/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A7LKPMP3/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/4ED55N1Q/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pm2p5_seasalt_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_wet_deposition/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pm2p5_seasalt_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_wet_deposition>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including \"content_of_atmosphere_layer\" are used. The mass is the total mass of the particles. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. \"Pm2p5 aerosol\" is an air pollutant with an aerodynamic diameter of less than or equal to 2.5 micrometers. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Wet deposition\" means deposition by precipitation. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::A7LKPMP3";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_pm2p5_seasalt_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_wet_deposition"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

