        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Sr\" means the element \"strontium\" and \"90Sr\" is the isotope \"strontium-90\" with a half-life of 1.02e+04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::95SAHUOK";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_90Sr"@en;
