        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Cm\" means the element \"curium\" and \"244Cm\" is the isotope \"curium-244\" with a half-life of 6.42e+03 days."@en;
