<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0836/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0836";
        dc:date                "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0836";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-06-26 15:24:29.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0836/4/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0836/3/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0836/1/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0836/2/>;
        pav:version            "4";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_geostrophic_sea_water_x_velocity> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_geostrophic_sea_water_x_velocity/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "4";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/RFVL/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G920/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G920/>;
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. A velocity is a vector quantity. \"x\" indicates a vector component along the grid x-axis, positive with increasing x. \"Geostrophic\" indicates that geostrophic balance is assumed, i.e. that the pressure gradient force and the Coriolis force are balanced and the large scale fluid flow is parallel to the isobars. The quantity with standard name surface_geostrophic_sea_water_x_velocity is the sum of a variable part, surface_geostrophic_sea_water_x_velocity_assuming_mean_sea_level_for_geoid, and a constant part due to the stationary component of ocean circulation."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0836";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_geostrophic_sea_water_x_velocity"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UVAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N619/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N619";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 15:23:07.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N619";
        dc:isReplacedBy        <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GOP20L7L/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 15:23:07.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N619/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N619/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "true";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_dust_dry_aerosol_due_to_gravitational_settling> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_dust_dry_aerosol_due_to_gravitational_settling/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/ATPC/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G107/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/G107/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area.  The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used.  \"Aerosol\" means the suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets).  Aerosol takes up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the aerosol. \"Dry aerosol\" means aerosol without water. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a  single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity  named by omitting the phrase.  \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time.  The sum of turbulent deposition and gravitational settling is dry deposition."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N619";
        skos:note              "deprecated"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_dust_dry_aerosol_due_to_gravitational_settling"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GOP20L7L/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::GOP20L7L";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::GOP20L7L";
        dc:replaces            <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N619/>;
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GOP20L7L/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GOP20L7L/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_dust_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_gravitational_settling/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_dust_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_gravitational_settling>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used. The mass is the total mass of the particles. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. Aerosol particles take up ambient water (a process known as hygroscopic growth) depending on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. \"Dry aerosol particles\" means aerosol particles without any water uptake. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. The sum of turbulent deposition and gravitational settling is dry deposition. \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::GOP20L7L";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_atmosphere_mass_content_of_dust_dry_aerosol_particles_due_to_gravitational_settling"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0554/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0554";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0554";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0554/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/longitude/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/longitude> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/B39/current/longitude/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/ALAT/>;
        skos:definition        "Longitude is positive eastward; its units of degree_east (or equivalent) indicate this explicitly. In a latitude-longitude system defined with respect to a rotated North Pole, the standard name of grid_longitude should be used instead of longitude. Grid longitude is positive in the grid-eastward direction, but its units should be plain degree."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0554";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "longitude"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/DEGE/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/97LNFXQ2/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::97LNFXQ2";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::97LNFXQ2";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/97LNFXQ2/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_77mGe_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_77mGe_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Ge\" means the element \"germanium\" and \"77mGe\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"germanium-77\" with a half-life of 6.27e-04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::97LNFXQ2";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_77mGe_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CD12V8PY/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CD12V8PY";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CD12V8PY";
