        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Sn\" means the element \"tin\" and \"121Sn\" is the isotope \"tin-121\" with a half-life of 1.12e+00 days."@en;
