        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Ac\" means the element \"actinium\" and \"227Ac\" is the isotope \"actinium-227\" with a half-life of 7.87e+03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::0DCOAXHA";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_227Ac_in_air"@en;
