        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Permafrost is soil or rock that has remained at a temperature at or below zero degrees Celsius throughout the seasonal cycle for two or more years. \"Thickness\" means the vertical extent of a layer."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV16A33";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "permafrost_layer_thickness"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/98PAWYYW/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::98PAWYYW";
        dc:date                "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::98PAWYYW";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/98PAWYYW/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/soil_mass_content_of_nitrogen/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/soil_mass_content_of_nitrogen>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"soil content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including \"content_of_soil_layer\" are used."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::98PAWYYW";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "soil_mass_content_of_nitrogen"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KMP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/07XQ0799/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::07XQ0799";
        dc:date                "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::07XQ0799";
        pav:authoredOn         "2024-05-20 20:39:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/07XQ0799/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/07XQ0799/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/tendency_of_air_temperature_due_to_longwave_heating_from_volcanic_ambient_aerosol_particles/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/tendency_of_air_temperature_due_to_longwave_heating_from_volcanic_ambient_aerosol_particles>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. Air temperature is the bulk temperature of the air, not the surface (skin) temperature. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. The term \"longwave\" means longwave radiation. \"Aerosol\" means the system of suspended liquid or solid particles in air (except cloud droplets) and their carrier gas, the air itself. \"Ambient_aerosol\" means that the aerosol is measured or modelled at the ambient state of pressure, temperature and relative humidity that exists in its immediate environment. \"Ambient aerosol particles\" are aerosol particles that have taken up ambient water through hygroscopic growth. The extent of hygroscopic growth depends on the relative humidity and the composition of the particles. To specify the relative humidity and temperature at which the quantity described by the standard name applies, provide scalar coordinate variables with standard names of \"relative_humidity\" and \"air_temperature\". Volcanic aerosols include both volcanic ash and secondary products such as sulphate aerosols formed from gaseous emissions of volcanic eruptions. It is strongly recommended that a variable with this standard name should have the attribute units_metadata=\"temperature: difference\", meaning that it refers to temperature differences and implying that the origin of the temperature scale is irrelevant, because it is essential to know whether a temperature is on-scale or a difference in order to convert the units correctly (cf. https://cfconventions.org/cf-conventions/cf-conventions.html#temperature-units)."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::07XQ0799";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "tendency_of_air_temperature_due_to_longwave_heating_from_volcanic_ambient_aerosol_particles"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KPRS/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A8LKMXA5/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::A8LKMXA5";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::A8LKMXA5";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/A8LKMXA5/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_140Ba_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_140Ba_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Ba\" means the element \"barium\" and \"140Ba\" is the isotope \"barium-140\" with a half-life of 1.28e+01 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::A8LKMXA5";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_140Ba_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Z5FQITOY/>
