<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ECFAHXEC/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::ECFAHXEC";
        dc:date                "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::ECFAHXEC";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/ECFAHXEC/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/canadian_fire_weather_index/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/canadian_fire_weather_index>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The Canadian Fire Weather Index (CFWI) is a numerical rating of potential frontal fire intensity from the Canadian Forest Fire Index System. It indicates fire intensity by combining the rate of spread with the amount of fuel being consumed and is also used for general public information about fire danger conditions. It is a function of wind speed, temperature, relative humidity, and precipitation. The calculation accounts for multiple layers of flammable material on the ground as well as fine fuels above the surface, combined with the expected rate of spread of fire. The index is open ended."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::ECFAHXEC";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "canadian_fire_weather_index"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PBL8WDD1/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::PBL8WDD1";
        dc:date                "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::PBL8WDD1";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PBL8WDD1/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PBL8WDD1/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/platform_heave/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/platform_heave>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Heave is a displacement along the local vertical axis. Heave is relative to the \"at rest\" position of the platform with respect to the axis of displacement. The \"at rest\" position of the platform may change over time. The standard name platform_heave should be chosen only if the sign convention of the data is unknown. For cases where the sign convention of the heave is known, a standard name of platform_heave_down or platform_heave_up should be chosen, as appropriate. A \"platform\" is a structure or vehicle that serves as a base for mounting sensors. Platforms include, but are not limited to, satellites, aeroplanes, ships, buoys, instruments, ground stations, and masts."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::PBL8WDD1";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "platform_heave"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/T6L3SREI/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::T6L3SREI";
        dc:date                "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::T6L3SREI";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-10-15 12:56:49.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/T6L3SREI/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/T6L3SREI/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/partial_pressure_of_methane_in_sea_water/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/partial_pressure_of_methane_in_sea_water>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The partial pressure of a dissolved gas in sea water is the partial pressure in air with which it would be in equilibrium. The partial pressure of a gaseous constituent of air is the pressure that it would exert if all other gaseous constituents were removed, assuming the volume, the temperature, and its number of moles remain unchanged. The chemical formula for methane is CH4."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::T6L3SREI";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "partial_pressure_of_methane_in_sea_water"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/PASX/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N65/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N65";
        dc:date                "2019-02-04 14:52:10.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N65";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-02-04 14:52:10.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N65/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N65/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/atmosphere_mass_content_of_hypochlorous_acid/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/atmosphere_mass_content_of_hypochlorous_acid>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HLAT/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"atmosphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used. The chemical formula for hypochlorous acid is HOCl."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N65";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "atmosphere_mass_content_of_hypochlorous_acid"@en;
