<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7MDP5HXC/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::7MDP5HXC";
        dc:date                "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::7MDP5HXC";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-08-06 12:15:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/7MDP5HXC/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_surface_tertiary_swell_wave_directional_spread/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_surface_tertiary_swell_wave_directional_spread>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The quantity with standard name sea_surface_tertiary_swell_wave_directional_spread is the directional width of the tertiary swell wave component of a sea. Swell waves are waves on the ocean surface and are the low frequency portion of a bimodal wave frequency spectrum. The tertiary swell wave is the third most energetic swell wave. Directional spread is the (one-sided) directional width within a given sub-domain of the wave directional spectrum, S(t,x,y,f,theta) where t is time, x and y are horizontal coordinates (such as longitude and latitude), f is frequency and theta is direction. For a given mean wave (beam) direction the quantity approximates half the root mean square width about the beam axis, as derived either directly from circular moments or via the Fourier components of the wave directional spectrum."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::7MDP5HXC";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_surface_tertiary_swell_wave_directional_spread"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UAAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TY6BSI8K/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::TY6BSI8K";
        dc:date                "2017-07-24 14:36:59.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::TY6BSI8K";
        pav:authoredOn         "2017-07-24 14:36:59.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/TY6BSI8K/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/sea_floor_depth_below_geopotential_datum/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/sea_floor_depth_below_geopotential_datum>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Depth_below_X\" means the vertical distance below the named surface X. The \"geopotential datum\" is any estimated surface of constant geopotential used as a datum i.e. a reference level; for the geoid as a datum, specific standard names are available. To specify which geoid or geopotential datum is being used as a reference level, a grid_mapping variable should be attached to the data variable as described in Chapter 5.6 of the CF Convention."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::TY6BSI8K";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "sea_floor_depth_below_geopotential_datum"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/V6L18VRV/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::V6L18VRV";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::V6L18VRV";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/V6L18VRV/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_radioactivity_content_of_115mAg/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_radioactivity_content_of_115mAg>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ag\" means the element \"silver\" and \"115mAg\" is the metastable state of the isotope \"silver-115\" with a half-life of 1.97e-04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::V6L18VRV";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_115mAg"@en;
