        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Pu\" means the element \"plutonium\" and \"235Pu\" is the isotope \"plutonium-235\" with a half-life of 1.81e-02 days."@en;
