<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PCH8Q2F1/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::PCH8Q2F1";
        dc:date                "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::PCH8Q2F1";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-07-03 16:09:23.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/PCH8Q2F1/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/maximum_over_coordinate_rotation_of_sea_ice_horizontal_shear_stress/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/maximum_over_coordinate_rotation_of_sea_ice_horizontal_shear_stress>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs. Axial stress is the symmetric component of the tensor representing the gradient of internal forces (e.g. in ice). Shear stress refers to off-diagonal element(s) of the stress tensor (a single element for horizontal shear stress). \"Horizontal\" refers to the local horizontal in the location of the sea ice, i.e., perpendicular to the local gravity vector. Each of the stress components is defined with respect to a frame of reference. \"Coordinate rotation\" refers to the range of all possible orientations of the frame of reference. The shear stress has a maximum value relative to one of these orientations. The second invariant of stress, often referred to as the maximum shear stress, is the maximum over coordinate rotations of the shear stress."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::PCH8Q2F1";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "maximum_over_coordinate_rotation_of_sea_ice_horizontal_shear_stress"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/NTPM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0574/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFSN0574";
        dc:date                "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFSN0574";
        pav:authoredOn         "2006-09-26 18:12:43.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0574/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/land_binary_mask/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/land_binary_mask>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/COAS/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/HBEX/>;
        skos:definition        "X_binary_mask has 1 where condition X is met, 0 elsewhere. 1 = land, 0 = sea."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFSN0574";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "land_binary_mask"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GJC9B0YH/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::GJC9B0YH";
        dc:date                "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::GJC9B0YH";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-05-15 09:59:16.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/GJC9B0YH/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/surface_upward_mass_flux_of_carbon_dioxide_expressed_as_13C_due_to_plant_respiration/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/surface_upward_mass_flux_of_carbon_dioxide_expressed_as_13C_due_to_plant_respiration>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Upward\" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. The chemical formula for carbon dioxide is CO2. \"C\" means the element carbon and \"13C\" is the stable isotope \"carbon-13\", having six protons and seven neutrons. The specification of a physical process by the phrase \"due_to_\" process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. Plant respiration is the sum of respiration by parts of plants both above and below the soil. It is assumed that all the respired carbon dioxide is emitted to the atmosphere. The term \"plants\" refers to the kingdom of plants in the modern classification which excludes fungi. Plants are autotrophs i.e. \"producers\" of biomass using carbon obtained from carbon dioxide."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::GJC9B0YH";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_upward_mass_flux_of_carbon_dioxide_expressed_as_13C_due_to_plant_respiration"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/KSP2/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N1/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CFV10N1";
        dc:date                "2008-10-21 10:00:00.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CFV10N1";
        pav:authoredOn         "2008-10-21 10:00:00.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFV10N1/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/altimeter_range> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/altimeter_range/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/ASLV/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/H021/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P64/current/H021/>;
        skos:definition        "An altimeter operates by sending out a short pulse of radiation and measuring the time required for the pulse to return from the sea surface; this measurement is used to calculate the distance between the instrument and the sea surface.  That measurement is called the \"altimeter range\" and does not include any range corrections."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CFV10N1";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "altimeter_range"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/41V7KNT5/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::41V7KNT5";
        dc:date                "2015-07-08 15:41:36.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::41V7KNT5";
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-07-08 15:41:36.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/41V7KNT5/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/radius_of_tropical_cyclone_maximum_sustained_wind_speed/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/radius_of_tropical_cyclone_maximum_sustained_wind_speed>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The great circle distance measured from the tropical cyclone center to the region of sustained 1-minute duration maximum wind speed, as defined by the standard name, tropical_cyclone_maximum_sustained_wind_speed."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::41V7KNT5";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radius_of_tropical_cyclone_maximum_sustained_wind_speed"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/ULAA/> .

