        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Sb\" means the element \"antimony\" and \"125Sb\" is the isotope \"antimony-125\" with a half-life of 9.97e+02 days."@en;
