        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Ag\" means the element \"silver\" and \"111Ag\" is the isotope \"silver-111\" with a half-life of 7.50e+00 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::5WHTCL3T";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_111Ag"@en;
