        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Rh\" means the element \"rhodium\" and \"106Rh\" is the isotope \"rhodium-106\" with a half-life of 3.46e-04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::JV4KKW4W";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "radioactivity_concentration_of_106Rh_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Y7NOULT3/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::Y7NOULT3";
        dc:date                "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::Y7NOULT3";
        pav:authoredOn         "2023-04-24 17:39:19.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/Y7NOULT3/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_ratio_of_moisture_to_dry_soil/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_ratio_of_moisture_to_dry_soil>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The quantity with standard name mass_ratio_of_moisture_to_dry_soil is also known as the water content of a soil or the wet-basis gravimetric moisture content. It is the ratio of the mass of water (liquid and solid) to the mass of the dried sample.The phrase \"ratio_of_X_to_Y\" means X/Y. It may be expressed as a fraction, a percentage, or any other dimensionless representation of a fraction."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::Y7NOULT3";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_ratio_of_moisture_to_dry_soil"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N497/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N497";
        dc:date                "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N497";
        pav:authoredOn         "2019-03-04 17:29:46.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N497/2/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N497/1/>;
        pav:version            "2";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mole_concentration_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mole_concentration_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "2";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/AAMN/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G161/>;
        skos:definition        "\"Mole concentration\" means number of moles per unit volume, also called \"molarity\", and is used in the construction \"mole_concentration_of_X_in_Y\", where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical or biological species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". \"Nox\" means a combination of two radical species containing nitrogen and oxygen: NO+NO2. The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N497";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mole_concentration_of_nox_expressed_as_nitrogen_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/MLM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CRK2STEM/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CRK2STEM";
        dc:date                "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CRK2STEM";
        pav:authoredOn         "2025-05-13 08:28:42.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CRK2STEM/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/blue_component_of_toa_outgoing_shortwave_flux_expressed_as_rgb_color/>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "Blue corresponds to the blue component of the RGB model. The term \"shortwave\" means shortwave radiation. The abbreviation \"toa\" means top of atmosphere. The TOA outgoing shortwave flux is the reflected and scattered solar radiative flux, i.e., the \"upwelling\" TOA shortwave flux, sometimes called the \"outgoing shortwave radiation\" or \"OSR\". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \"flux\" implies per unit area, called \"flux density\" in physics. The intensity is scaled relative to a reference intensity or the maximum possible value. It is recommended that the variable attributes valid_min and valid_max or valid_range are used to denote the range of possible values (e.g., 0 to 1, 0 to 255, 0 to 65,535). The radiation wavelength or frequency range for blue can be denoted as bounds of a scalar coordinate variable."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CRK2STEM";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "blue_component_of_toa_outgoing_shortwave_flux_expressed_as_rgb_color"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UUUU/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/N4AII95X/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::N4AII95X";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
