        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The surface called \"surface\" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Pu\" means the element \"plutonium\" and \"238Pu\" is the isotope \"plutonium-238\" with a half-life of 3.15e+04 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::O1K82YP2";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "surface_radioactivity_content_of_238Pu"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BQSM/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N299/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::CF12N299";
        dc:date                "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::CF12N299";
        pav:authoredOn         "2015-01-07 16:23:38.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N299/3/>;
        pav:hasVersion         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N299/2/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CF12N299/1/>;
        pav:version            "3";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/mass_concentration_of_nmvoc_expressed_as_carbon_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/mass_concentration_of_nmvoc_expressed_as_carbon_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "3";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:broader           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P02/current/OCAA/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P04/current/G141/>;
        skos:definition        "Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The phrase \"expressed_as\" is used in the construction A_expressed_as_B, where B is a chemical constituent of A. It means that the quantity indicated by the standard name is calculated solely with respect to the B contained in A, neglecting all other chemical constituents of A. \"nmvoc\" means non methane volatile organic compounds; \"nmvoc\" is the term used in standard names to describe the group of chemical species having this classification that are represented within a given model. The list of individual species that are included in a quantity having a group chemical standard name can vary between models. Where possible, the data variable should be accompanied by a complete description of the species represented, for example, by using a comment attribute."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::CF12N299";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "mass_concentration_of_nmvoc_expressed_as_carbon_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/UKMC/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8FOA3TWE/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::8FOA3TWE";
        dc:date                "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        dc:identifier          "SDN:P07::8FOA3TWE";
        pav:authoredOn         "2018-02-12 16:53:18.0";
        pav:hasCurrentVersion  <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/8FOA3TWE/1/>;
        pav:version            "1";
        void:inDataset         <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/.well-known/void>;
        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:sameAs             <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/standard_name/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_206Tl_in_air/> , <http://mmisw.org/ont/cf/parameter/integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_206Tl_in_air>;
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The phrase \"integral_wrt_X_of_Y\" means int Y dX. The data variable should have an axis for X specifying the limits of the integral as bounds. The phrase \"wrt\" means \"with respect to\". \"Radioactivity\" means the number of radioactive decays of a material per second. \"Radioactivity concentration\" means radioactivity per unit volume of the medium. \"Tl\" means the element \"thallium\" and \"206Tl\" is the isotope \"thallium-206\" with a half-life of 2.91e-03 days."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::8FOA3TWE";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
        skos:prefLabel         "integral_wrt_time_of_radioactivity_concentration_of_206Tl_in_air"@en;
        skos:related           <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P06/current/BSM3/> .

<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/1SLC8V4I/>
        rdf:type               skos:Concept;
        dce:identifier         "SDN:P07::1SLC8V4I";
