        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "The construction \"moles_of_X_per_unit_mass_in_Y\" is also called \"molality\" of X in Y, where X is a material constituent of Y. A chemical species or biological group denoted by X may be described by a single term such as \"nitrogen\" or a phrase such as \"nox_expressed_as_nitrogen\". The chemical formula for hydrogen peroxide is H2O2."@en;
        skos:notation          "SDN:P07::9UYOFIKP";
        skos:note              "accepted"@en;
